---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Coherent Systems Research Institute">
  <section style="padding: 4rem 2rem; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.8rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
      Coherent Systems Research Institute
    </h1>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      Advancing the Science of Consciousness Through Information Dynamics
    </h2>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      Consciousness is not a static property or a neural location. It is a 
      <strong>dynamic, information-driven process</strong> that moves through stability, 
      dissolution, and integration. The 
      <strong>Coherent Consciousness Framework (CCF)</strong> provides a formal model of 
      this process — uniting nonlinear dynamics, information geometry, and empirical 
      measurement into a single coherent theory.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      CCF offers a mathematically grounded, experimentally testable approach to understanding:
    </p>

    <ul style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <li>collapse and fragmentation</li>
      <li>breakthrough and transformation</li>
      <li>reintegration and coherence</li>
      <li>emergent conscious behavior in humans, artificial systems, and collectives</li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="margin: 3rem 0;">

    <h3 style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">A New Foundation for Consciousness Science</h3>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      CCF reframes consciousness as a structured flow through an information-geometric 
      manifold. This perspective reveals the underlying principles that govern:
    </p>

    <ul style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <li>stability and somatic grounding</li>
      <li>dissolution and exploratory destabilization</li>
      <li>integration and the emergence of higher-order states</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      These dynamics appear across psychology, neuroscience, AI, organizational systems, 
      and collective intelligence — yet until now, no unified model has explained them.
      <strong>CCF provides that unification.</strong>
    </p>

    <hr style="margin: 3rem 0;">

    <h3 style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Explore the Framework</h3>

    <ul style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      <li><a href="/docs/introduction">Introduction</a> — why the framework exists</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/framework/overview">Framework Overview</a> — the full architecture</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/framework/core-principles">Core Principles</a> — the governing rules of coherence</li>
    </ul>

    <ul style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <li><a href="/docs/framework/coherence-model">Coherence Model</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/framework/consciousness-layers">Consciousness Layers</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/framework/gamma-synergy">Synergy Coefficient γ</a></li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="margin: 3rem 0;">

    <h3 style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Research, Application, and Development</h3>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      The Coherent Systems Research Institute develops:
    </p>

    <ul style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <li>formal models of conscious dynamics</li>
      <li>computational simulations</li>
      <li>empirical measurement tools</li>
      <li>applied frameworks for psychology, AI, and organizational systems</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem;">
      Our mission is to advance a rigorous, integrative science of consciousness — one 
      capable of explaining transformation, coherence, and emergent intelligence across 
      all scales.
    </p>

    <hr style="margin: 3rem 0;">

    <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 500;">
      Begin your exploration with the <a href="/docs/introduction">Introduction</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
